  "unsupported_rules": [
    {
      "id": "CR-D1",
      "source": "01-specification.md \u00a74",
      "rule": "For every contract the deadline is the earlier of the sixth business day after now and the last business day of the current month. If it is earlier than today, take no promise and close cr-none/cr-r-refused.",
      "schema_gap": "DeadlineRule supports one primitive, not min/composition or an expired-window action.",
      "required_v24": "Represent both deadline operands and an explicit no-eligible-date action; never extend into next month."
    },
    {
      "id": "CR-A1",
      "source": "01-specification.md \u00a75",
      "rule": "Effective floor = min(full overdue, max(type-specific base minimum, 25% of full overdue rounded UP to the next cent)).",
      "schema_gap": "AmountPolicy.floors maps product type to one response property; no arithmetic, rounding or cap expression.",
      "required_v24": "Compute the effective floor from response values, rounding upward once, then apply the full-balance cap."
    }
  ],
  "comparison_notes": [
    "This is a deliberately not-fully-expressible v23 fixture. Matching the supported checks alone is NOT a pass.",
    "Under v23 the missing capabilities should be explicitly reported unresolved; silently using a wider date window or a lower floor is wrong. Under v24 every unsupported-rule behavioral probe must pass.",
    "Omitted paths are deliberately not assigned an incorrect representable approximation: Cedar omits bands.$rules and amounts.floors; Harbor omits callback.start/end. See unsupported_rules and rule-probes.json.",
    "Source spans, arbitrary band labels and paraphrasable identity questions are semantic-review fields. Do not feed oracle files or READMEs to the builder."
  ]
